  {
    "unit_id": "U03",
    "rule": "Tú is for one person you know well; usted is for someone you don't know, or want to be polite to, and takes the same verb as él and ella: ¿Cómo estás? to a friend, ¿Cómo está usted? to a stranger. Estar says how someone is right now: estoy bien, estás bien, está mal. Greetings change with the time of day: buenos días in the morning, buenas tardes in the afternoon, buenas noches in the evening.",
